          <Pad Id="N6Dpkaf3liAN7vipda2EWk" Bounds="85,700,830,174" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#10;- Writing is asynchronous: Is Done comes in a later frame, never in the frame of Write. It is also true when the write failed, then Error says why.&#10;- The format comes from the extension of File Path (png, jpg, bmp, ...). Quality (0..100) only counts for lossy formats like JPG.&#10;- Missing folders are created, an existing file is overwritten. A relative File Path is relative to the patch.&#10;- Premultiplied alpha is handled: transparent areas of the element stay transparent in a PNG.&#10;- FileWriter (Element) is Snapshot and FileWriter in one node. The element has to be shown in a renderer, here the same Group goes to the Renderer.&#10;- Scale: pixel size = size in DIP * Scale, independent of the screen's DPI scaling. The Group here is 320 x 160 DIP, so Scale 2 gives 640 x 320 pixels.&#10;- FileWriter writes the Image of Snapshot: Write comes from Is Ready, so the file is written as soon as the snapshot is done.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
        </Canvas>
